.py:19 test_dispatch_records_instruction_tokens never exercises the Codex dispatch path (daemon._dispatch_fresh_fix / the main dispatch loop). It only calls spawn.with_instruction_tokens(spawn.packet_run_meta(packet), prompt, packet) directly on hand-built strings -- the same assertion as tests/test_spawn.py::test_run_worker_records_instruction_tokens. The spec explicitly asked for a test with 'the executor patched' that verifies packet_meta handed to executor.start carries instruction_tokens; that wiring in daemon.py:573-579 and :862-875 (spawn.with_instruction_tokens(spawn.packet_run_meta(packet), prompt, packet) actually being called before dispatch) is never invoked or asserted. A regression that drops the with_instruction_tokens call from either dispatch site, or swaps its arguments, would not be caught.\ntests/test_spawn.py:1055 test_review_packet_records_candidate_tokens_before_diff_budget never calls review_packet(). It builds a packet via spawn._role_packet('## diff\\nshort', 'dead', 'test', candidate_tokens=99, candidate_known=True) with candidate_tokens supplied manually, so it never verifies that review_packet() itself computes candidate_tokens=len(raw_diff)//4 from the diff before bounded_diff truncates it (spawn.py review_packet, ~line 530-533). If review_packet were changed to pass the already-bounded diff's length instead of raw_diff, this test would still pass.\ntests/test_spawn.py:1062 test_run_worker_records_instruction_tokens never calls run_worker(). It duplicates the same with_instruction_tokens(packet_run_meta(packet), prompt, packet) arithmetic check used by the daemon test, so the actual role branches in run_worker (review/spec_review/execute/scout, spawn.py ~800-825) that are supposed to merge instruction_tokens into t['packet_meta'] are never exercised.\norchestrator/spawn.py:9 _PACKET_BUILD_META is a module-level dict keyed by packet content hash that is written on every packet()/_role_packet() call and never evicted or bounded. In a long-running daemon process this grows without limit for the life of the process (unbounded memory growth), though it does not affect correctness of a single run.\n```\n\nKeep every original acceptance criterion:\n- tests/test_spawn.py::test_section_meta_splits_named_sections passes\n- tests/test_spawn.py::test_packet_run_meta_reports_sections_and_presented_tokens passes\n- tests/test_spawn.py::test_review_packet_records_candidate_tokens_before_diff_budget passes\n- tests/test_spawn.py::test_run_worker_records_instruction_tokens passes\n- tests/test_daemon.py::test_dispatch_records_instruction_tokens passes\n- tests/test_executor.py::test_fallback_context_measures_only_the_packet passes\n- tests/test_executor.py::test_repair_delta_headings_are_not_packet_sections passes\n- tests/test_executor.py::test_bare_delta_yields_unmeasured_context passes\n- tests/test_bus.py::test_log_run_derives_context_from_packet_meta passes\n- tests/test_context_scorecard.py::test_amplification_by_section_groups_by_goal passes\n- tests/test_context_scorecard.py::test_rows_per_role_and_unmeasured_count passes\n- orchestrator scorecard --context prints per-role and per-goal tables; docs/context-economy/01-telemetry.md exists; rendered prompts are byte-identical to before\n\nImplement the smallest fix within the task scope and verify all acceptance criteria.\n\n\nPlanner note (15:35): all four comments are valid. Make test_dispatch_records_instruction_tokens drive daemon._dispatch_fresh_fix (or the dispatch loop) with executor patched and assert the logged run's context.instruction_tokens; make test_review_packet_records_candidate_tokens_before_diff_budget call review_packet() with a raw diff longer than the budget and assert candidate_tokens == len(raw_diff)//4 while presented is smaller; make test_run_worker_records_instruction_tokens call run_worker() with the worker/executor patched for at least the review and execute branches; bound _PACKET_BUILD_META (an OrderedDict evicting beyond 512 entries, or keyed per process with a clear on log) and add a one-line test. Keep prompts byte-identical (acceptance: 'rendered prompts are byte-identical to before').",
